From 9ad6291a5aa78961e6fa6b1d70231186af49da58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:35:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] fix(mailbox): synthesize a mailer config when only
 [mailbox] is configured
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Making [mailer] optional left a crash behind. Gitea composes mail from the
[mailer] settings regardless of what sends it — the From address, the subject
prefix, header overrides, the display-name template — so once MailEnabled()
let the notification path run without [mailer], the first issue comment
dereferenced a nil setting.MailService and panicked.

Rather than nil-check twenty call sites, a mailbox-only instance now gets a
MailService with sane defaults and a sender of gitea@DOMAIN. It is marked with
the "mailbox" protocol so nothing mistakes it for a transport: no upstream
sender is built from it, and OUTBOUND_MODE = relay still refuses to run
without a real [mailer].

Also documents that a notification lands in the webmail INBOX when the
recipient's account email is on the mailbox domain, which is what makes issue
and pull-request mail readable over IMAP alongside everything else.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
